From: Corios00 <52224974+Corios00@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 04:59:50 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] The sun shadows' caster pass builds its stats lines only
 when they are asked for

`extract_casters` runs in the extract every frame the look's shadows are on, once for every
model mesh in the world (hidden ones too). For each it built the line `WOW_SHADOW_STATS` prints,
whether the list was armed or not: a `format!` with float formatting for every caster, a second
`format!` for every mesh that doesn't cast, and a material lookup for every hidden or out-of-range
mesh, all thrown away. The extract runs with the main world stopped, so it lands straight on the
frame. The lines are now built only while the list is armed (once a second, with the variable set).

A caster whose material is still parked (`model_render::lazy`: a mesh the camera hasn't looked at
yet) had its whole material cloned every frame (a `StandardMaterial` and its extension, every
handle's reference count up and down) to read three fields. Its verdict is now read in place under
the table's lock, and the value is copied only for the stats list.

What casts and how is unchanged: the same verdicts, from the same fields, in the same order.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
